sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila ananassae Turing wavenumber at 2.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 74.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 integrates Schnakenberg kinetics (a=0.11, b=1.15, Dv/Du=19.7) on a 128×96 periodic grid. The fastest linear mode is placed at 2.106 µm by the choice of dx. The saturated FFT wavelength is 2.030 µm. The growth GIF is 12 frames at 960×640 and modulates the public-domain female plate. There is no parameter sweep, no integrated ablation, no specimen-versus-render segmentation, and no Pearson/RMSE/KS fit. Overall 74.8/100 (faithfulness 71.0, reproducibility 83.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b527a03f163994a07bd008d5b308a54ec56094a4; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 46, Morphometric validation 58, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_ananassae_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0.py at b527a03f163994a07bd008d5b308a54ec56094a4, image/png, 555209 B, 1200×800 px, artifact_sha256 4a7d8f8ac9bfbd853e01074a802305b51f7028a66c35ec910e013d96c1cfda86 (sha256 4a7d8f8ac9bfbd853e01074a802305b51f7028a66c35ec910e013d96c1cfda86), spec_fingerprint cb48fb2dc3693d0cac7caeab627f7cf256ca041c37d25c1fbbe642b593156101. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: cb48fb2dc3693d0cac7caeab627f7cf256ca041c37d25c1fbbe642b593156101; artifact_sha256: 4a7d8f8ac9bfbd853e01074a802305b51f7028a66c35ec910e013d96c1cfda86; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_ananassae_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_ananassae_specimen.png=e3f07821c201b2b5..., datasets/drosophila_ananassae_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_ananassae_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=2768c7dcb983c315...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics. | D. ananassae is a sequenced ananassae-subgroup species (12 Genomes Consortium 2007); geological age in this slot is 0 Ma. | Ready, Hanson and Benzer (1976) describe the retinal lattice at a scale of a few micrometres. | Gompel et al. (2005) show the biarmipes wing spot is a multi-cell yellow pattern; Wittkopp, Carroll and Kopp (2003) review coarser abdominal pigment.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.11, b=1.15, Dv/Du=19.7 and dx chosen so argmax Re σ(k) equals 2.106 µm. | Diffusivity ratios versus D. americana (139 µm) and D. biarmipes (96 µm) under λ ∝ √D. | Activator field painted as a luminance modulation on the Wikimedia plate.; transfer_boundary: 2.106 µm is this slot's assigned detail-scale wavelength, not a published Turing-wavelength measurement on ananassae cuticle.; does_not_claim: The transverse sex comb and the optomotor-blind chiasma are not claimed as products of this 2.1 µm mode. | The adult body outline is the vendored plate, not an output of the reaction-diffusion field. | Slot 2841's 85 µm power-law parameters were not reused. | The Lean file was not executed by a Lean kernel on this machine.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add a parameter-regime sweep (diffusion ratio and a kinetic scale factor) and record how wavelength moves.",
            "remediation needed: Integrate the equal-diffusion control and a linear-kinetics ablation; do not stop at the sign of σ(k).",
            "remediation needed: Kernel-check the Lean file when a Lean 4 binary is available.",
            "remediation needed: Report Pearson r, RMSE, and a KS statistic for the wavelength law, with value unequal to the reference.",
            "remediation needed: Segment the real plate and the GIF last frame and compare foreground fraction, circularity, aspect, and coherency." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.748"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 builder-assessor, pass 1 (no second assessor on this run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

